/-- Paper mirror-prox objective generated by an abstract Bregman-like divergence on a
candidate carrier and an ambient evaluation map.
Layer: Model | Concept: Prox
Proof: (definitional construction; mirror-prox objective combining linear term + Bregman regularizer)
Source: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for Machine Learning,
  Eq. (3.2.5).
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
noncomputable def paperMirrorObjective
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (V : P → P → ℝ) (eval : P → E) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) : ℝ :=
  γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ + V x y

/-- Expanded formula for the abstract paper mirror-prox objective.
Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (prox objective formula)
Proof: expand the staged objective definition.
Source: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for Machine Learning,
  Eq. (3.2.5).
Used in: stochastic mirror descent objective formula bridge
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem paperMirrorObjective_def
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (V : P → P → ℝ) (eval : P → E) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) :
    paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ y = γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ + V x y := by
  rfl

/-- Literal mirror-prox objective with an interior base and separate candidate carrier.

Defines the prox objective `γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ + Vlit x y` used when the
Bregman term is supplied literally on an interior/base point and a candidate.

Layer: Model | Concept: Prox
Proof: (definitional construction; literal mirror-prox objective as a weighted
  linear inner-product term plus the supplied Bregman divergence term)
Source: Mathlib inner product space notation and real scalar algebra APIs
Used in: stochastic mirror descent prox-step literal objective expansion for
  interior-base mirror updates
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, stochastic mirror descent -/
noncomputable def literalMirrorObjective
    {E Xint P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (Vlit : Xint → P → ℝ) (eval : P → E) (x : Xint) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) : ℝ :=
  γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ + Vlit x y

/-- Expanded formula for the literal interior-base mirror-prox objective.

The literal mirror objective at candidate `y` is exactly the linearized loss term
`γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ` plus the supplied literal divergence from the base point `x`.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (literal mirror objective expansion)
Proof: by rfl after unfolding literalMirrorObjective.
Source: Mathlib inner product space notation and real algebra APIs
Used in: stochastic mirror descent prox-step objective normalization
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem literalMirrorObjective_def
    {E Xint P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (Vlit : Xint → P → ℝ) (eval : P → E) (x : Xint) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) :
    literalMirrorObjective Vlit eval x g γ y = γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ + Vlit x y := by
  rfl

/-- The literal interior-base mirror objective is the carrier paper mirror objective after
pulling the divergence back along the base-point map.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (literal prox objective bridge)
Proof: unfold both objective definitions and rewrite the divergence term with the
  point-map compatibility hypothesis.
Source: Mathlib simplification and rewriting APIs for real inner-product expressions
Used in: stochastic mirror descent bridge from literal prox objectives to carrier paper objectives
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for Machine
  Learning, stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem literalMirrorObjective_eq_paperMirrorObjective
    {E Xint P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (V : P → P → ℝ) (Vlit : Xint → P → ℝ) (toPoint : Xint → P) (eval : P → E)
    (hV : ∀ x y, V (toPoint x) y = Vlit x y)
    (x : Xint) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) :
    literalMirrorObjective Vlit eval x g γ y =
      paperMirrorObjective V eval (toPoint x) g γ y := by
  rw [literalMirrorObjective_def, paperMirrorObjective_def, hV x y]

/-- Continuity of the abstract paper mirror-prox objective in the candidate point.
Layer: Model | Gap: Level 1 (prox objective continuity)
Proof: compose the continuous linear oracle term with the continuous divergence section.
Source: Mathlib continuity API for inner-product spaces.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem paperMirrorObjective_continuous
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) :
    Continuous (paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ) := by
  have hinner : Continuous (fun y : P => ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ) :=
    continuous_const.inner heval
  have hlin : Continuous (fun y : P => γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ) :=
    continuous_const.mul hinner
  have hsection : Continuous (fun y : P => V x y) :=
    hV.comp (continuous_const.prodMk continuous_id)
  simpa [paperMirrorObjective] using hlin.add hsection

/-- Abstract argmin predicate for the paper mirror-prox step.
Layer: Model | Concept: Prox
Proof: (definitional construction; predicate asserting a point realises a mirror-step argmin)
Source: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for Machine Learning,
  Eq. (3.2.5).
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
def IsMirrorStep
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (V : P → P → ℝ) (eval : P → E) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (z : P) : Prop :=
  IsMinOn (paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ) Set.univ z

/-- Expanded form of the abstract paper mirror-step argmin predicate.
Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (prox argmin predicate)
Proof: rewrite `IsMinOn` over `Set.univ`.
Source: Mathlib order/topology argmin predicates.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem isMirrorStep_iff
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    (V : P → P → ℝ) (eval : P → E) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (z : P) :
    IsMirrorStep V eval x g γ z ↔
      ∀ y : P, paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ z ≤
        paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ y := by
  rw [IsMirrorStep, isMinOn_univ_iff]

/-- Compactness/continuity existence route for an abstract paper mirror-prox argmin.
Layer: Model | Gap: Level 1 (compact prox argmin existence)
Proof: apply Mathlib's compact extreme-value theorem to the continuous staged objective.
Source: Mathlib `IsCompact.exists_isMinOn`.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem mirrorStep_exists_compact
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hcompact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set P))
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) :
    ∃ z : P, IsMirrorStep V eval x g γ z := by
  rcases hcompact.exists_isMinOn
      (⟨x, trivial⟩ : (Set.univ : Set P).Nonempty)
      (paperMirrorObjective_continuous hV heval x g γ).continuousOn with
    ⟨z, _hz, hzmin⟩
  exact ⟨z, hzmin⟩

/-- Canonical compact argmin object for the abstract paper mirror-prox objective.
Layer: Model | Concept: Prox
Proof: (definitional construction; argmin selector for the mirror-prox objective)
Source: Mathlib compact extreme-value theorem.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
noncomputable def proxStepArgmin
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hcompact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set P))
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) :
    {z : P // IsMirrorStep V eval x g γ z} :=
  let h := mirrorStep_exists_compact hcompact hV heval x g γ
  ⟨Classical.choose h, Classical.choose_spec h⟩

/-- Canonical compact argmin selector for the abstract paper mirror-prox objective.
Layer: Model | Concept: Prox
Proof: (definitional construction; canonical mirror-prox update operator)
Source: Mathlib compact extreme-value theorem.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
noncomputable def proxStep
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hcompact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set P))
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) : P :=
  (proxStepArgmin hcompact hV heval x g γ).1

/-- The canonical compact argmin selector satisfies the abstract paper mirror-step
predicate.
Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (prox selector specification)
Proof: project the proof component from the chosen argmin subtype.
Source: Mathlib compact extreme-value theorem.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem proxStep_isMirrorStep
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hcompact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set P))
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) :
    IsMirrorStep V eval x g γ (proxStep hcompact hV heval x g γ) := by
  exact (proxStepArgmin hcompact hV heval x g γ).2

/-- The canonical compact argmin selector minimizes the abstract paper mirror-prox
objective.
Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (prox selector minimizes)
Proof: expand the argmin predicate supplied by the selector specification.
Source: Mathlib compact extreme-value theorem.
Used in: stochastic mirror descent compact prox selector
Book citation: `book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec/steps/0/math`
Origin algorithm: FOML stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem proxStep_minimizes
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hcompact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set P))
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) :
    paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ (proxStep hcompact hV heval x g γ) ≤
      paperMirrorObjective V eval x g γ y := by
  exact (isMirrorStep_iff V eval x g γ
    (proxStep hcompact hV heval x g γ)).1
      (proxStep_isMirrorStep hcompact hV heval x g γ) y

/-- Joint continuity of the paper mirror-prox objective in the base point, oracle
vector, step size, and candidate point.

The objective `(x,g,γ,y) ↦ γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫ + V x y` is continuous whenever
the Bregman term is jointly continuous and the model evaluation map is
continuous.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 1 (mirror-prox objective joint continuity)
Proof: compose product projections with the continuous evaluation and Bregman
  maps, then combine Mathlib continuity rules for inner products,
  multiplication, and addition.
Source: Mathlib topology of product spaces and continuous inner-product APIs
Used in: stochastic mirror descent prox-step objective continuity
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for Machine Learning, stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem paperMirrorObjective_joint_continuous
    {P E : Type*} [TopologicalSpace P] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) :
    Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P =>
      SOptLib.paperMirrorObjective V eval q.1.1 q.1.2.1 q.1.2.2 q.2) := by
  have hg : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P => q.1.2.1) :=
    continuous_fst.comp (continuous_snd.comp continuous_fst)
  have hγ : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P => q.1.2.2) :=
    continuous_snd.comp (continuous_snd.comp continuous_fst)
  have hy : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P => eval q.2) :=
    heval.comp continuous_snd
  have hinner : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P =>
      ⟪q.1.2.1, eval q.2⟫_ℝ) :=
    hg.inner hy
  have hlin : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P =>
      q.1.2.2 * ⟪q.1.2.1, eval q.2⟫_ℝ) :=
    hγ.mul hinner
  have hx : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P => q.1.1) :=
    continuous_fst.comp continuous_fst
  have hz : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P => q.2) :=
    continuous_snd
  have hVcomp : Continuous (fun q : (P × E × ℝ) × P => V q.1.1 q.2) :=
    hV.comp (hx.prodMk hz)
  simpa [SOptLib.paperMirrorObjective] using hlin.add hVcomp

/-- A strongly convex mirror objective has at most one mirror-prox minimizer.

If two candidates minimize the same mirror objective and both satisfy the mirror
variational inequality, the symmetric Bregman identity makes the summed
first-order inequalities bound the symmetric Bregman gap by zero. The strict
lower bound then forces zero evaluation distance, and injectivity of `eval`
identifies the minimizers.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 1 (unique argmin for strongly convex mirror objective)
Proof: add the two variational inequalities, rewrite their sum with the
  symmetric Bregman identity, use the norm-square lower bound to force
  `‖eval z - eval z'‖ = 0`, then apply injectivity of `eval`.
Source: Mathlib inner product space algebra and real norm/order APIs
Used in: stochastic mirror descent prox-step unique argmin for the mirror objective
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem paperMirrorObjective_argmin_unique_of_strict_bregman
    {P E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval grad : P → E} {obj : P → ℝ}
    (heval_inj : Function.Injective eval)
    (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (z z' : P)
    (hvariational : ∀ {a b : P}, (∀ y : P, obj a ≤ obj y) →
      0 ≤ ⟪γ • g + grad a - grad x, eval b - eval a⟫_ℝ)
    (hsymm : ∀ a b : P,
      V a b + V b a = ⟪grad b - grad a, eval b - eval a⟫_ℝ)
    (hlower : ∀ a b : P, ‖eval a - eval b‖ ^ 2 ≤ V a b + V b a)
    (hzmin : ∀ y : P, obj z ≤ obj y)
    (hz'min : ∀ y : P, obj z' ≤ obj y) :
    z = z' := by
  have hzvar : 0 ≤ ⟪γ • g + grad z - grad x, eval z' - eval z⟫_ℝ :=
    hvariational hzmin
  have hz'var : 0 ≤ ⟪γ • g + grad z' - grad x, eval z - eval z'⟫_ℝ :=
    hvariational hz'min
  have hsum_nonneg := add_nonneg hzvar hz'var
  have hsum_eq :
      ⟪γ • g + grad z - grad x, eval z' - eval z⟫_ℝ +
        ⟪γ • g + grad z' - grad x, eval z - eval z'⟫_ℝ =
          -(V z z' + V z' z) := by
    rw [hsymm z z']
    have hrev : eval z - eval z' = -(eval z' - eval z) := by
      abel
    rw [hrev, inner_neg_right]
    simp [inner_add_left, inner_sub_left, inner_smul_left]
  have hsym_nonpos : V z z' + V z' z ≤ 0 := by
    linarith
  have hnormsq_le_zero : ‖eval z - eval z'‖ ^ 2 ≤ 0 :=
    le_trans (hlower z z') hsym_nonpos
  have hnorm_zero : ‖eval z - eval z'‖ = 0 := by
    have hsquare : ‖eval z - eval z'‖ ^ 2 = 0 :=
      le_antisymm hnormsq_le_zero (sq_nonneg ‖eval z - eval z'‖)
    exact sq_eq_zero_iff.mp hsquare
  apply heval_inj
  have hsub : eval z - eval z' = 0 := norm_eq_zero.mp hnorm_zero
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp hsub

/-- A chosen compact mirror-prox step satisfies the expanded objective inequality.

For the canonical compact mirror-prox selector, the selected prox point minimizes the
literal objective `γ * ⟪g, eval ·⟫_ℝ + V x ·` against every candidate `y`.

Layer: Model | Gap: Level 0 (expanded prox-step minimization inequality)
Proof: unfolds `paperMirrorObjective` and reuses `proxStep_minimizes` by `simpa`.
Source: Mathlib compactness and continuous real-valued optimization APIs
Used in: stochastic mirror descent prox-step optimality in expanded source form
Book citation: book/FOML/StochasticMirrorDescent.json#/algorithm_spec
Origin algorithm: Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for
  Machine Learning, stochastic mirror descent -/
theorem proxStep_minimizes_expanded
    {E P : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace P]
    {V : P → P → ℝ} {eval : P → E}
    (hcompact : IsCompact (Set.univ : Set P))
    (hV : Continuous (fun p : P × P => V p.1 p.2))
    (heval : Continuous eval) (x : P) (g : E) (γ : ℝ) (y : P) :
    γ * ⟪g, eval (proxStep (V := V) (eval := eval) hcompact hV heval x g γ)⟫_ℝ +
        V x (proxStep (V := V) (eval := eval) hcompact hV heval x g γ) ≤
      γ * ⟪g, eval y⟫_ℝ + V x y := by
  simpa [SOptLib.paperMirrorObjective] using
    (proxStep_minimizes (V := V) (eval := eval) hcompact hV heval x g γ y)

